  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Whist. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: 'Whist is the classic English partnership trick-taking game and ancestor of Bridge. 4 players, 2 teams. 52 cards, 13 each. Last card dealt (to dealer) turned face-up = trump. Eldest hand leads. Follow suit. Each trick over 6 = 1 point. Honours (A-K-Q-J of trump): 3 held = 2pts, 4 held = 4pts. Game to 5 (British) or 7 (American). Rubber = best of 3.',
    objective: 'As a team, collect the required consecutive points before the opponents score and reset progress.',
    gameplay: 'Two partnerships play a Minnesota Whist-style trick game. Scoring is the key distinction: only one team has points at a time, so the win total must be built in consecutive scoring hands.',
    keyRules: [
      'Variant of Minnesota Whist.',
      'Only one team can have points at a time.',
      'Points needed to win must be collected consecutively.',
    ],
